<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="060" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Office job status lives in a static in-memory dictionary — it does not survive a restart or a second instance</title>
    <phase>4 Parity, deploy, close</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 058 AND 067 merge — 058 removes attachment/share members that also touch the job path, and 067 lands the creator-OID schema change this task consumes. RE-SCOPED 2026-09-21: two persisted fields and the client's terminal-error handling are now in scope. See the RE-SCOPE block in background.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>A live correctness defect on the deployed save path, not a refactor. Tags include bff-api. The storage decision is architectural (ADR-009 Redis-first) and the extraction is a hot-path change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The storage decision is a genuine architectural choice (Redis per ADR-009 vs the existing Dataverse ProcessingJob row vs accepting in-memory with a documented constraint), and it interacts with the already-shipped SSE stream and idempotency spine. Not a mechanical move.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>`OfficeService.cs` / `OfficeEndpoints.cs` hot-path, shared with `unified-access-control-r2`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>058,067</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, office, data, reliability, refactor, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Office job status is held in a process-wide static dictionary. Decide and implement the correct store, then extract the job-status and SSE cluster out of OfficeService.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. The storage decision comes first; the extraction is the cleanup that follows it.</role>

  <goal>A user polling a job's status gets a truthful answer after an app restart and from any instance. OfficeService no longer owns job-status storage or SSE streaming.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-09-19 by this project's pre-wrap-up `/code-review`.

      `OfficeService.cs:74`:

          private static readonly ConcurrentDictionary&lt;Guid, JobStatusResponse&gt; _jobStore = new();

      That is **all** Office job state, held in one process's memory, written at 8+ sites (`:408`, `:498`,
      `:648`, `:663`, `:694`, `:741`, `:796`, …). The pane polls it at
      `src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts:669`
      (`GET /api/office/jobs/{jobId}`) and streams it via `/jobs/{jobId}/stream`.

      **This is not theoretical.** `spaarke-bff-dev` was stopped and restarted three times on 2026-09-19
      during deployment; every in-flight job's status was discarded silently. A user polling across that window
      sees a job vanish, not fail. The same happens on any scale-out: instance B has never heard of instance
      A's job.

      `OfficeService.cs:1487` already carries the marker `TRACKED: GitHub #229 - Replace with Dataverse query
      once ProcessingJob exists` — and `ProcessingJob` **does** now exist; `IProcessingJobService` is already a
      constructor dependency of this very class, and `_documentPersistence.CheckForExistingJobAsync` already
      queries it for idempotency. So the durable store the comment is waiting for is already wired in.
    </background>
    <notes>
      **DECIDE THE STORE BEFORE MOVING ANY CODE.** Three candidates, and the task must pick one with reasons:
      (a) the existing Dataverse `ProcessingJob` row — already queried on the idempotency path, already a
      dependency, no new infrastructure; (b) Redis per ADR-009 (Redis-first for cross-request state) — better
      fit for high-frequency polling, but new infrastructure on this path; (c) keep in-memory and document the
      constraint honestly — only defensible if job status is genuinely ephemeral, which the SSE reconnect path
      suggests it is not.

      Evaluate (a) first: it needs no new dependency and the idempotency path already proves the query works.

      **DO NOT silently keep in-memory.** If (c) is chosen, the pane must be told — a status that can vanish
      needs a defined client behaviour, not a 404 the user reads as failure.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-009">Redis-first for cross-request cached state. `IMemoryCache`-shaped in-process storage for data that must survive a request is the documented anti-pattern — a static dictionary is a stronger form of it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register any new collaborator as a concrete class; do not add a single-implementation interface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 039 / 047">The idempotency spine and the content-hash version-save key are already correct and shipped. Do NOT change key derivation. This task changes WHERE status is stored, never HOW a job is identified.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 029">The SSE stream and the post-save AI refresh depend on job records. Their behaviour must be unchanged.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>ADDED 2026-09-21 — `Result.Artifact` IS PERSISTED. `OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs:846-855` persists only Status/Progress/CurrentStage/ErrorMessage; the artifact (document id) written into `_jobStore` at `OfficeService.cs:749`, `:827`, `:1457` is never stored. Without this, a durable store still returns a `Completed` job with no document id.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADDED 2026-09-21 — CLIENT TERMINAL ERROR. `useSaveFlow.ts:755-776` handles `Completed`-with-artifact and error; **neither branch matches `Completed`-without-artifact**, so `cleanup()` runs, `flowState` stays `'processing'`, and the pane sits on the job card forever with no error. The SSE path does the same (`OfficeService.cs:3165-3172` emits `FormatJobComplete(jobId, null, null)` → `useSaveFlow.ts:622` `if (documentId)` is false). Make both paths treat `Completed`-without-artifact as a TERMINAL ERROR the user can see.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADDED 2026-09-21 — the creator OID from task 067 is carried by the chosen store, so `JobOwnershipFilter` enforces ownership on the durable path too. If 067 chose a Dataverse column, confirm the store reads it.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADDED 2026-09-21 — BEHAVIOURAL ACCEPTANCE, not structural: restart the app mid-save and show the pane reports a definite outcome (success with a document, or a visible error). "The static dictionary is gone" is not sufficient evidence that the user-visible defect is fixed.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADDED 2026-09-21 — the sibling defects NOT in this task's scope are named in the task note with their owning task: `OfficeProfileDispatcher` fire-and-forget and `JobStatusService._jobSequences` (both task 068). This prevents 060 being later cited as having fixed them.</criterion>
    <criterion>REPRODUCE-FIRST: a test proves status is lost across a simulated process boundary (new service instance / cleared store) BEFORE the fix, and survives it after. Record the red verbatim in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion>The storage decision is written down with its reasons and the two rejected alternatives, in the task note, BEFORE implementation.</criterion>
    <criterion>`_jobStore` as a `private static` field is gone; job status reads and writes go through the chosen store.</criterion>
    <criterion>Job status survives a service-instance replacement in test, and the SSE stream still delivers the same event sequence.</criterion>
    <criterion>Job-status and SSE members move to a new concrete `OfficeJobStatusService`, registered unconditionally in `OfficeModule`; `IOfficeService` is UNCHANGED (interface-last, as in 059).</criterion>
    <criterion>`OfficeService` constructor parameter count DROPS. State before/after. (AMENDED 2026-09-21: the line-count half of this criterion is removed — CLAUDE.md §11.5 forbids gating on LOC. The job-status extraction is the one genuinely correct cut per the architecture review; judge it on cohesion, not size.)</criterion>
    <criterion>All existing job-status, idempotency (039) and AI-refresh (029) tests pass UNMODIFIED. Name them. A test needing modification means behaviour changed — stop and explain.</criterion>
    <criterion>Full BFF suite green; ArchTests 191/191; publish size vs a fresh master build; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion>`OfficeService.cs:1487`'s stale `TRACKED: GitHub #229` comment is removed or corrected — the ProcessingJob it waits for already exists.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the chosen store cannot preserve the SSE stream's event ordering or its reconnect/`lastEventId` semantics, STOP and escalate. Job-status durability must not be bought by breaking the stream task 029 depends on.</trigger>
    <trigger>If evidence shows job status is genuinely ephemeral and in-memory is correct, STOP and escalate rather than implementing (c) unilaterally — that decision changes the client contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Confirm 058 merged. /conflict-check.</step>
    <step>Reproduce the loss; record the red.</step>
    <step>Evaluate the three stores, starting with the existing ProcessingJob row; write the decision and the rejected alternatives down.</step>
    <step>Implement the store change with the existing tests unmodified.</step>
    <step>Extract the job-status and SSE cluster into `OfficeJobStatusService`; register concretely.</step>
    <step>Gates, then `notes/060-job-status-store-and-extraction.md` with the decision record and before/after metrics.</step>
  </steps>

  <relevant-files>
    <file role="edit">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
    <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeJobStatusService.cs</file>
    <file role="edit">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/OfficeModule.cs</file>
    <file role="read">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts</file>
    <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/060-job-status-store-and-extraction.md</file>
  </relevant-files>

  <justification>
    <existing>`IProcessingJobService` is ALREADY a constructor dependency of `OfficeService`, and `OfficeDocumentPersistence.CheckForExistingJobAsync` already queries the Dataverse ProcessingJob row on the idempotency path (`OfficeService.cs:245`). Grep evidence: `_jobStore` appears at `:74` plus 8 write sites; `IProcessingJobService` is injected at `:78`.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for storage — extend the existing ProcessingJob path rather than add a store. No for the service class: the goal is to REMOVE surface from `OfficeService`, and `OfficeJobStatusService` is a peer of the existing `OfficeDocumentPersistence` / `OfficeStorageUploader` collaborators.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user who saves a document and polls its status across an app restart is told the job does not exist — observed on 2026-09-19, when three restarts discarded all in-flight job state. On scale-out, a poll routed to a second instance returns 404 for a job that is running. Both present as "the save vanished," which is the failure class this project spent tasks 039 and 047 eliminating from the save spine.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeJobStatusService.cs</file>
    <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/060-job-status-store-and-extraction.md</file>
  </outputs>
</task>
